@ 32.1.1 - Proto-Chatino to Papabuco Chatino
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Upson, B.W., and Robert E. Longacre (1965), “Proto-Chatino Phonology”. International Journal of American Linguistics 31(4):312 – 322
	t > ɾ / :{ _uwhen unstressed, _ẽwhen unstressed }:
	t > ɾ / _a
	t > t͡ʃ / _{e,iʔ}
	t > ʃ / i_i
	t > s // in cluster with š (presumably:[ʃ])
	tʲ > s / _u
	tʲ > t͡ʃ
	k > ɡ / a_a
	kʷ > ɾ / #_ek
	kʷ > b
	ʔ > ∅ (?)
	{c,t͡ʃ} > ʃ
	s > t͡ʃ (in certain cases? Not a lot of data available on this one)
	l > {lʲ,n} “under obscure conditions”
	n > nʲ
	nʲ > l / #_i
	h > d / _a (…lolwut)
	h > t / (…again, lolwut)
	j > nʲ “under obscure conditions (PC morphophonemics?)”
	i > e / t͡ʃ_
	ı̃ > i
	e > a / :{ _lwhen unstressed, _ʔnwhen unstressed }:
	e > i / :{ kʲ_ when stressed, nt_ when stressed }:
	e > i / in a few data set͡s where obscure morphological development͡s (in the ultimate or penultimate syllable) have resulted in regressive assimilation of vowel quality
	ẽ > a / tʲ_
	ẽ > i / h_
	ẽ > i / in :[+long -stress]
	ẽ > e
	a > {i,e} “under special conditions”